      {
        "id": 115227,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-24T14:19:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think it was aimed at the card leaving play before you place Ambuscade on the map, so Ambuscade wouldn't be placed on the map.</p><p>That does not work, the card goes first.</p><p>Also I believe that when that was possible in playtesting the ruling was going to be that if cloak left play you had to immediately place Ambuscade on the map.</p><p>So I would stick with that, even though I don't think it is possible to remove the card from play with Ambuscade off the map at this point.</p>",
